# Customer Churn Prediction Using Machine Learning

## Project Overview
This project predicts whether a customer is likely to leave a company using Machine Learning techniques.

## Objective
To analyse customer data and predict customer churn using classification algorithms.

## Dataset
- Total customer records: 7,043
- Features: Customer demographics, services, contract details and charges.
- Target variable: Churn

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Joblib

## Data Preprocessing
- Checked missing values.
- Converted TotalCharges into numeric format.
- Removed missing records.
- Applied One-Hot Encoding.
- Split data into training and testing sets.

## Machine Learning Algorithms
1. Logistic Regression
2. Random Forest Classifier

## Model Performance
Logistic Regression:
- Accuracy: 80.31%
- F1-score: 0.6071

Random Forest:
- F1-score: 0.5604

Logistic Regression achieved a higher F1-score in this experiment.

## Project Files
- customer_churn_model.pkl – Saved trained model.
- feature_names.json – Saved input feature names.

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates how Machine Learning can be used to predict customer churn and help businesses understand customer retention.

